According to my dictionary, a "kil" (single l) is a "waterdeep, body of
water between two heights or sandbanks, between shallows or riverbanks,
etc.".

A second meaning is a riverbed, this often appears in topographical names,
my dictionary mentions the "Dordtse Kil" as an example.

The third meaning is a "trog" (which I guess translates to English as a
"trough"), a very long, deep part of the oceans (usually located on the
border of two tectonic plates).

